-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version], s 121B — additional tax on high incomes, in Part 7.
-- Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHAT THIS SECTION DOES. (a) charges 3% on the part of an individual's taxable income
-- above an amount printed as 640,000 (as at 2017). (a1) charges a further 2% on the part
-- of the individual's taxable income FROM CAPITAL SOURCES above the same amount, measured
-- on that income alone. (e) defines "taxable income" for the section more widely than s 1
-- does: it adds real-estate betterment (with a residential-apartment threshold) and takes
-- out the inflationary amounts.
--
-- WHICH TAX YEARS IT ANSWERS: 2026 ONWARD, with the s 121B(a) amount supplied by the caller
-- (NOTES.md, assumption A1). The section's last amendment is of 5785 (src:4455) and the
-- sources do not say from which tax year it applies, so tax years before 2026 are declined.
-- The amount in (a) is an income ceiling that s 120B adjusts (s 120A, src:4335): for 2026
-- and 2027 it is the 1 January 2024 figure after rounding (s 120B(e)(1)); from 2028 it is
-- that figure re-adjusted and rounded under s 120B(d), which is not encoded. The figure the
-- consolidation gives in an editorial note (721,560 for 2024-2027) is not encoded; the tests
-- supply it, labelled as such.
-- The residential-apartment threshold in (e) is printed as 5,385,285, which the note says is
-- nominal for 2025 and unchanged in 2026; from 2027 it moves under s 9(c2) of the Real Estate
-- Taxation Law, which is not encoded, so a residential sale in 2027 or later is declined, and
-- any other case is still answered. Version 0.2.0 (repair 03-O1): the threshold is answered
-- for 2026 only. 2025 is declined like the rest of s 121B for 2025, because whether the 5785
-- amendment that wrote this figure applies to tax year 2025 is the same open question.

§ `Section 121B — additional tax on high incomes`
-- src:4455 | סעיף 121ב – מס נוסף על הכנסות גבוהות [תיקון: תשע״ג־10, תשע״ז־6, תשפ״ה־2]

§§ `The amount in 121B(a)`

-- The text prints 640,000 "nominal for 2017": the base the s 120B adjustments start from.
-- No rule here reads it; the figure in force is an input (see the header).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(a) (source line 4456), with its note "(נקוב לשנת 2017)"
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount printed in section 121B(a), as at 2017` MEANS 640_000

-- The route s 120B gives to the figure in force, for a caller who holds the s 120B facts
-- for this amount (`kind` = `an income ceiling`).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(a) (source line 4456), s 120A "תקרות הכנסה" (source line 4335), s 120B (source lines 4338-4345)
GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `An amount on 1 January of a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount in section 121B(a) in force, under section 120B, from` `the facts` MEANS
    `s 120B — the amount in force in the tax year` `the facts`

§§ `121B(e) — "taxable income", and "taxable income from a capital source"`

-- src:4461 | (ה) בסעיף זה –
-- src:4462 | ”הכנסה חייבת“ – הכנסה חייבת כהגדרתה בסעיף 1 וכמשמעותה בסעיף 89, למעט סכום אינפלציוני כהגדרתו בסעיף 88 וסכום אינפלציוני כהגדרתו בסעיף 47 לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ולרבות שבח כמשמעותו בחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ואולם לגבי מכירת זכות במקרקעין בדירת מגורים כהגדרתה בחוק האמור – רק אם שווי מכירתה עולה על 5,385,285 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2025; בשנת 2026, 5,385,285 ש״ח)] והמכירה אינה פטורה ממס לפי כל דין; הסכום האמור יתואם בהתאם להוראות סעיף 9(ג2) לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ולעניין זה יהיה המדד הבסיסי כאמור באותו סעיף המדד שפורסם ביום המדד שפורסם ביום ז׳ בשבט התשפ״ז (15 בינואר 2027);

-- "Excluding the inflationary amount as defined in section 88": an item counts net of it.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) "הכנסה חייבת" (source line 4462)
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income for section 121B in` `the item` MEANS
    `the item`'s `amount` MINUS `the item`'s `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`

-- The residential-apartment threshold. The text prints 5,385,285 and the note says it is
-- the figure for 2025 and, unchanged, for 2026. It is then adjusted under s 9(c2) of the
-- Real Estate Taxation Law from a base index published on 15 January 2027.
-- Version 0.2.0 (repair 03-O1, INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md observation O1): until then this
-- helper answered TRUE for 2025 while the section's rule below declines every year before
-- 2026, so one note was read both ways. The note says what the figure is in 2025, not that
-- s 121B as amended in 5785 reaches tax year 2025; the deposited text does not say from which
-- tax year that amendment applies (amendment 276, Sefer HaChukim 3342, is not deposited;
-- NOTES.md assumption A1 and question 4). So this helper now declines 2025 and earlier with
-- the section's own refusal: TRUE for 2026, FALSE from 2027, declined before 2026.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) (source line 4462), with its note "(נקוב לשנת 2025; בשנת 2026, 5,385,285 ש״ח)"; s 121B amendment list at source line 4455
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the text fixes the residential-apartment sale value for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    IF   `the tax year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model`
    ELSE `the tax year` EQUALS 2026

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) (source line 4462): "יתואם בהתאם להוראות סעיף 9(ג2) לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין"; that Law is not in this row's sources
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) from 2027 moves under section 9(c2) of the Real Estate Taxation Law, which is not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) from 2027 moves under section 9(c2) of the Real Estate Taxation Law, which is not encoded in this model"

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B — amendment list at source line 4455; the tax year from which the 5785 amendment applies is not in the deposited source
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model"

-- Version 0.2.0 (03-O1): 2025 is declined, as the section's rule declines it; the arms are
-- now in year order, so the refusal before 2026 is reached first, by name.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) (source line 4462)
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the tax year` LESS THAN 2026
           THEN `section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model`
           IF `the text fixes the residential-apartment sale value for tax year` `the tax year`
           THEN 5_385_285
           OTHERWISE `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) from 2027 moves under section 9(c2) of the Real Estate Taxation Law, which is not encoded in this model`

-- "Including betterment ... but for the sale of a right in a residential apartment, only if
-- its sale value exceeds [the threshold] and the sale is not exempt from tax under any
-- law". The residential limb is consulted ONLY for a residential sale, so a non-residential
-- sale never reaches the threshold (and never its 2027 refusal). The "not exempt" condition
-- belongs to the residential limb alone (fork F9). "Exceeds" (עולה על) is strict.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) "הכנסה חייבת" (source line 4462)
GIVEN `the sale`     IS A `A sale of a right in real estate`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the betterment on` `the sale` `counts for section 121B in tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
       NOT `the sale`'s `in a residential apartment`
    OR (    `the sale`'s `sale value` GREATER THAN `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) for tax year` `the tax year`
        AND NOT `the sale`'s `exempt from tax under any law`)

-- Counted net of its inflationary amount under s 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law; a sale
-- whose betterment does not count contributes nothing, its inflationary amount included
-- (fork F9).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) "הכנסה חייבת" (source line 4462)
GIVEN `the sale`     IS A `A sale of a right in real estate`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income for section 121B from` `the sale` `in tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    IF   `the betterment on` `the sale` `counts for section 121B in tax year` `the tax year`
    THEN `the sale`'s `betterment` MINUS `the sale`'s `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law`
    ELSE 0

-- src:4460 | (ד) הוראות סעיף 8(ג) יחולו לגבי ההכנסות הקבועות בו, בחישוב ההכנסה החייבת לעניין סעיף זה.
-- (d) is an input convention here: the items of income are taken after any s 8(c)
-- spreading the taxpayer requested (ito-il03-nouns.l4). s 8(c) itself is not in this row.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(d) (source line 4460), s 121B(e) "הכנסה חייבת" (source line 4462)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income for section 121B of` `the individual` MEANS
         sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the taxable income for section 121B in` i) (`the individual`'s `items of income`))
    PLUS sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the taxable income for section 121B from` s `in tax year` (`the individual`'s `tax year`)) (`the individual`'s `sales of rights in real estate`))

-- src:4463 | ”הכנסה חייבת ממקור הוני“ – הכנסה חייבת, למעט כל אחת מאלה:
-- src:4464 | (1) הכנסה לפי סעיף 2(1) או (2);
-- src:4465 | (2) הכנסה מיגיעה אישית שאינה הכנסה כאמור בפסקה (1).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) "הכנסה חייבת ממקור הוני" (source lines 4463-4465)
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`from a capital source` `the item` MEANS
    NOT (   "(1)" ... `the item`'s `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`
         OR "(2)" ... `the item`'s `from personal exertion`)

-- Betterment under the Real Estate Taxation Law is neither s 2(1)/(2) income nor income
-- from personal exertion, so every counted betterment is from a capital source.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(e) "הכנסה חייבת ממקור הוני" (source lines 4463-4465)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income from a capital source for section 121B of` `the individual` MEANS
         sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `the taxable income for section 121B in` i)
                  (filter (GIVEN i YIELD `from a capital source` i) (`the individual`'s `items of income`)))
    PLUS sum (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the taxable income for section 121B from` s `in tax year` (`the individual`'s `tax year`)) (`the individual`'s `sales of rights in real estate`))

§§ `121B(a) — 3% above the amount`

-- src:4456 | (א) יחיד אשר הכנסתו החייבת בשנת המס עלתה על 640,000 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2017; בשנת 2023, 698,280 ש״ח; בשנים 2024–2027, 721,560 ש״ח)], יהיה חייב במס נוסף על חלק הכנסתו החייבת העולה על 640,000 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2017; ראו לעיל)], בשיעור של 3%.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(a) (source line 4456)
GIVEN `the taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount`         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121B(a) — the additional tax on` `the taxable income` `above` `the amount` MEANS
    IF   `the taxable income` GREATER THAN `the amount`
    THEN 3% TIMES (`the taxable income` MINUS `the amount`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `121B(a1) — a further 2% on capital-source income above the amount`

-- Measured on the capital-source income ALONE, against the same amount as (a), and in
-- addition to (a). The text says "ממקורות הוניים" (plural) where (e) defines the singular
-- term; read as the defined term (fork F11).
-- src:4457 | (א1) נוסף על האמור בסעיף קטן (א), יחיד אשר הכנסתו החייבת ממקורות הוניים בשנת המס עלתה על הסכום הקבוע באותו סעיף קטן, יהיה חייב במס נוסף על חלק הכנסתו החייבת ממקורות הוניים העולה על הסכום האמור, בשיעור של 2%.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(a1) (source line 4457)
GIVEN `the taxable income from a capital source` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount`                               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 121B(a1) — the additional tax on` `the taxable income from a capital source` `above` `the amount` MEANS
    IF   `the taxable income from a capital source` GREATER THAN `the amount`
    THEN 2% TIMES (`the taxable income from a capital source` MINUS `the amount`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `121B(b) — no advance payments under section 91(d)`

-- It changes how advances are paid, not how much additional tax is due; s 91(d) is not in
-- this row. Encoded as the answer the text gives to the one question it settles.
-- src:4458 | (ב) על הכנסה החייבת במס נוסף לפי סעיפים קטנים (א) או (א1) לא יחולו הוראות סעיף 91(ד) לעניין מקדמות.
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(b) (source line 4458)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 121B(b) — section 91(d) on advance payments applies to income chargeable to additional tax under (a) or (a1)` MEANS
    FALSE

§§ `121B(c) — notwithstanding any enactment — inert`

-- A priority clause. No other enactment is encoded in this row, so nothing here could
-- displace s 121B and the clause has nothing to act on.
-- src:4459 | (ג) הוראות סעיף זה יחולו על אף האמור בכל חיקוק.

§§ `Section 121B for an individual in a tax year`

@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B (source lines 4455-4465)
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B`
`a problem with the facts for section 121B of` `the individual` MEANS
    BRANCH IF any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `amount` LESS THAN 0) `the items`
           THEN JUST `an amount of income is negative`
           IF        any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88` LESS THAN 0) `the items`
                  OR any (GIVEN s YIELD s's `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` LESS THAN 0) `the sales`
           THEN JUST `an inflationary amount is negative`
           IF any (GIVEN s YIELD s's `betterment` LESS THAN 0 OR s's `sale value` LESS THAN 0) `the sales`
           THEN JUST `a betterment or a sale value is negative`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the items` MEANS `the individual`'s `items of income`
        `the sales` MEANS `the individual`'s `sales of rights in real estate`

-- The two refusals are settled first, in return position, so that neither can sit unforced
-- inside a RIGHT (phrasebook 11.8).
@ref Income Tax Ordinance s 121B(a), (a1), (e) (source lines 4456-4465)
GIVEN `the individual`                                         IS AN `An individual in a tax year`
      `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` NUMBER
`the additional tax under section 121B for` `the individual` `, with the amount in section 121B(a) at` `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the tax year` LESS THAN 2026
           THEN `section 121B for tax years before 2026 is not encoded in this model`
           IF        any (GIVEN s YIELD s's `in a residential apartment`) (`the individual`'s `sales of rights in real estate`)
              AND NOT `the text fixes the residential-apartment sale value for tax year` `the tax year`
           THEN `the residential-apartment sale value in section 121B(e) from 2027 moves under section 9(c2) of the Real Estate Taxation Law, which is not encoded in this model`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `a problem with the facts for section 121B of` `the individual`
               WHEN JUST `the problem` THEN LEFT `the problem`
               WHEN NOTHING            THEN RIGHT (`under (a)` PLUS `under (a1)`)
    WHERE
        `the tax year` MEANS `the individual`'s `tax year`
        `the amount`   MEANS `the amount in section 121B(a) in force in the tax year`
        `under (a)`    MEANS `s 121B(a) — the additional tax on` (`the taxable income for section 121B of` `the individual`) `above` `the amount`
        `under (a1)`   MEANS `s 121B(a1) — the additional tax on` (`the taxable income from a capital source for section 121B of` `the individual`) `above` `the amount`
